WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.270
This draft breaks my style guide on
purpose.

2
00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:06.107
Let's see what the workbench does with it.

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.467
Every red underline in the source is
something to fix.

4
00:00:10.517 --> 00:00:12.621
Select Check to see them all.

5
00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:18.060
The check names the rule behind each
finding, says why it matters,

6
00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.467
and shows the fix.

7
00:00:19.967 --> 00:00:24.551
One fix rewrites one line of the source,
and nothing else.

8
00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:27.552
Or take every fix at once.

9
00:00:27.602 --> 00:00:29.651
The draft now passes.

10
00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:33.691
The same code checks every document in my
library,

11
00:00:33.741 --> 00:00:36.815
so what you read here passed the same
test.

12
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.317
Write a document yourself, and watch it
get checked,

13
00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:43.791
at karandeshmukh.dev/workbench.
